WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.601
-The Biden administration
moved quickly

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.601
to stem the fallout
from the sudden collapse

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.868
of Silicon Valley Bank,
which has put a spotlight

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:09.400
on efforts
by the Trump administration

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.033
to weaken financial rules that
could've prevented the crisis.

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:13.968
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:18.167
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:20.267
As you may have heard by now,
financial markets

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.267
and the banking system
were roiled on Friday

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.968
after the sudden disintegration
of...

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.100
...which largely served

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.801
venture capitalists
and tech startups.

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.167
To many analysts
and finance gurus,

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.567
the collapse almost seemed
to come out of nowhere

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.067
and it happened very fast.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.968
-Silicon Valley Bank
collapsed today

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.868
after failing
to raise enough money

00:00:38.868 --> 00:00:40.901
to end its capital crisis.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.300
California regulators
shut down the bank

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.934
and put it in control
of the FDIC.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.701
-Silicon Valley Bank becoming

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:51.133
the second largest bank failure
in U.S. history.

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:54.167
-SVB, the 16th largest bank
in the U.S.,

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.367
with $175 billion in deposits,

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:59.701
is now the biggest American bank
to fail

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.934
since the 2008 financial crisis.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.801
Its customers
are primarily businesses

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.501
and investors
in the tech sector.

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:08.000
-The swift collapse
of Silicon Valley Bank

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.200
is the second largest financial
failure in U.S. history

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.267
and it took only 48 hours
to unfold.

00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:17.133
-Man, you got to give it
to Silicon Valley.

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:19.400
They know how to move fast
and break things.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.667
[ Laughter ]
Forty-eight hours!

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.167
They basically Amazon Prime'd
a bank collapse.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.267
[ Laughter ]
And, knowing Silicon Valley,
I wouldn't be surprised

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.767
if some tech startup
comes along,

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:30.601
promising even faster
bank collapses.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:31.634
"It's called...

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.167
You just download the app,

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.300
[ Laughter ]
press a button,
and watch as all your money

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:36.968
is instantly flushed
down a digital toilet.

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:37.767
Here, I'll show you."

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.367
[ Toilet flushes ]

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.434
"Honey, did you just lose
the kids' college money?"

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:47.934
Yes, but I got an NFT
of a cool plunger in sunglasses,

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:49.200
so win-win.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.000
Look, I don't want
to be a doomer,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.634
but situations like this
are exactly

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.300
why I keep all the money
right here in the desk drawer.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:59.100
What?! Where the hell did
all my money go?!

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.968
-I don't know, Seth.
It's a mystery.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:01.701
-Son of a gun.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.734
Wally, did you steal
all my savings?

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:07.200
-What?!
No!

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.067
I took the under on slaps
at the Oscars last night

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.534
and won big!
-Alright.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.100
The Treasury Department
and Federal Reserve

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.267
quickly responded to the news

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:17.234
by guaranteeing all deposits
at SVB,

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:18.667
which we'll get to in a minute,

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:21.167
but the news also gave us a real
contrast in leadership styles

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.567
from the current president
and the guy who preceded him.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:26.100
Joe Biden delivered remarks
from the White House,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.767
in an attempt to calm nervous
markets and worried Americans

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.234
after the collapse of the
country's 16th largest bank,

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.701
although he ended his remarks
on an odd note.

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:35.400
-Today, thanks
to the quick action

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.834
of my administration
over the past few days,

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:42.334
Americans can have confidence
that the banking system is safe.

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:45.133
Your deposits will be there
when you need them.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.734
Small businesses
across the country,

00:02:46.734 --> 00:02:49.067
that deposit accounts
at these banks

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.901
can breathe easier,
knowing they'll be able

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:53.834
to pay their workers
and pay their bills.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:56.667
And their hardworking employees
can breathe easier as well.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:03:01.000
All customers who had deposits
in these banks can rest assured.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.100
Rest assured
they'll be protected

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.667
and they'll have access
to their money, as of today.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.434
Every American
should feel confident

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:11.868
their deposits will be there,
if and when they need them.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.767
Look, the bottom line is this --

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:18.267
Americans can rest assured
that our banking system is safe.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.901
Your deposits are safe.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:22.634
Thank you, God bless you,
and may God protect our troops.

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.267
See you in California.

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:25.567
-"See you in California"?

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:28.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:31.501
If I was Silicon Valley Bank,
I would not like hearing that.

00:03:31.501 --> 00:03:32.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.434 --> 00:03:33.968
"Good news --
he bailed us out.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.534
Bad news -- he's on his way."

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:37.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:39.801
Biden's like a grandfather
telling a principal --

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.534
[ As Biden ]
You can rest assured
that my grandson

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.033
has pulled his last fire alarm.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.000
For one thing, he's not going
to be able to lift his arms

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.067
after he's done
cleaning the garage!

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:49.734
[ Laughter ]
Grandkid's sitting there,
mouthing to the principal,

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:51.734
[ Whispering ]
"Don't let this man
take me home with him."

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:53.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.467
Biden also made a point
of reassuring Americans

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.667
that taxpayers would not pay
for the bailout

00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:00.701
and that, while depositors
at SVB would be protected,

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:01.834
investors would not.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:04.834
-No losses will be borne
by the taxpayers.

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:05.934
Let me repeat that --

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.467
no losses will be borne
by the taxpayers.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:12.234
Investors in the banks
will not be protected.

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:14.133
They knowingly took a risk

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:15.801
and, when the risk
didn't pay off,

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.334
investors lose their money.

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:18.501
-Alright, seems fair.

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.234
Investors take risks,
knowing full well

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:21.601
there's a chance
they can lose all their money,

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:23.067
and that's what happened.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:25.367
-Hey, Seth, um,
can I borrow a few bucks?

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.000
-I'm sorry.
I don't have any on me.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.634
-Damn it! I shouldn't have
stolen all your money.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.801
[ Laughter and applause ]
-So it was you!

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:31.968
-Of course it was me.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:33.767
I invested it all
in Silicon Valley Bank.

00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:36.834
And I bet someone would slap
Jimmy Kimmel at the Oscars.

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:39.133
Damn you, Jimmy
and your unslappable charm!

00:04:39.133 --> 00:04:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:44.467
-So, Wally gets two cameras,
now?

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:47.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.767
[ Cheering ]

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:50.434
Great.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:52.133
Oh, good, I'm glad
you're so happy for him.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:54.801
[ Whistling ]

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:58.000
Anyway, so, as you heard there,
Biden used words like

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.234
safe, confidence,
and rest assured, over and over.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.734
And, while that's absolutely
the right thing

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.200
for a president to do
in this situation,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:07.267
generally speaking, I've never
personally felt assured

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:09.667
when a president has said
the words rest assured.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:10.701
[ Laughter ]
Unless it was Obama.

00:05:10.701 --> 00:05:12.634
He was the only president
who seemed calm,

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:15.133
while also making you feel
like a dork for being worried.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:18.067
[ As Obama ]
Now, I know some of you are
running around saying, "Hey!

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.133
My money's gone.

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.734
I, uh, can't get my money.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.501
Well, uh...listen up.

00:05:24.501 --> 00:05:25.901
You all need to chill
the [bleep] out.

00:05:25.901 --> 00:05:28.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.334
He'd be so cool about it,
you'd start thinking,

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:34.067
"Yeah, I don't need money,
especially since I got Plungie.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.067
[ Laughter and applause ]
He's got a pirate hat now.

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.734
Pirate hat doubles the value."

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:41.100
[ Laughter ]
In fact, Biden was so concerned
with projecting calm

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.634
that even the way he entered
the room for his speech

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:44.834
was very low-maintenance.

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:46.367
There was no pomp, no fanfare.

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:48.601
He didn't even have any staff
walk in with him.

00:05:48.601 --> 00:05:51.033
He just ambled in on his own,
closed the door,

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:52.567
and shuffled over to the podium,

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:54.868
like he was your next-door
neighbor popping in for a visit.

00:05:56.868 --> 00:06:00.067
[ Laughter and applause ]
-[ Mumbling ]

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:05.434 --> 00:06:07.567
I love that little shuffle step,

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.267
like a high school
history teacher

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:11.734
who's five minutes late
for class.

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:13.901
[ Laughter ]
"Like, oh, hey,
everybody's here.

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.801
Sorry, gang.
Big day in the teacher's lounge.

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:17.300
Mrs. Balducci's husband left her

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.567
and, based on how long it took
her to tell us the story,

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:21.033
I might understand why."

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.200
There's just no staff
around him,

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.501
no presidential fanfare.

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:27.300
He looked like he just walked
out of the bathroom

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.234
and now has
to improvise a speech.

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:31.501
[ Laughter ]
"Uh, first things first, uh...

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:32.868
don't go in there."

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.734
Nonetheless,
Biden did pretty much exactly

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:38.868
what you'd want a president
to do in this situation --

00:06:38.868 --> 00:06:39.968
take immediate action,

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:41.701
reassure Americans
everything will be okay.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.167
Much like the message former
President Donald Trump delivered

00:06:44.167 --> 00:06:45.901
on his social media website
over the weekend.

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:48.634
Trump is clearly aware
of the fact that, sometimes --

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:50.868
sometimes -- he has the tendency
to overreact,

00:06:50.868 --> 00:06:52.567
which could panic
nervous Americans

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:54.901
and send shock waves through the
financial markets for no reason.

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:56.934
So, instead of freaking
everyone out,

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:59.100
Trump projected calm
and confidence when he wrote

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.267
this very reassuring message
in all-caps --

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:06.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.567 --> 00:07:13.801
I mean, credit to him for not
ending it with...

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:17.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:18.834
Trump isn't just the guy
who shouts fire

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:20.234
in a crowded theater.
He's the guy

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:22.667
who lights the match, pours the
gasoline, and screams --

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:24.801
[ As Trump ]
There's a fire and there's
no point in leaving

00:07:24.801 --> 00:07:26.400
because I-I chained the exits.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:30.334
Fire. We hate fire,
don't we, folks?

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:32.200
[ Laughter ]
Very nasty. Not nice.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:33.367
Not nice, the fire.

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:35.267
I remember one time I was
in the Oval Office.

00:07:35.267 --> 00:07:37.100
I had a guy come up to me,
big guy, strong guy,

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.033
bolts in his neck...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:41.434
...tears pouring down his green,
monstrous face,

00:07:41.434 --> 00:07:43.467
and he said to me, he said,
"Mr. Trump,

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:44.801
fire bad."

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:47.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:49.934
And I said, "It's so true,
Frankenstein.

00:07:49.934 --> 00:07:51.133
...'s monster."

00:07:51.133 --> 00:07:51.901
[ Laughter ]
Now, look.

00:07:53.501 --> 00:07:56.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:56.801 --> 00:07:58.133
Very important.

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:01.834
[ Cheering and whistling ]

00:08:01.834 --> 00:08:04.267
A lot of people at home
right now going, "Oh, finally!"

00:08:04.267 --> 00:08:05.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.901 --> 00:08:07.367
Now, look, there's a lot to say

00:08:07.367 --> 00:08:09.200
about what happened
to Silicon Valley Bank.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.601
There's the fact that its
leaders and lobbyists pushed

00:08:11.601 --> 00:08:13.100
for more lenient
financial rules.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:15.367
There's the news
that the CEO sold

00:08:15.367 --> 00:08:16.734
over $3 million in stock

00:08:16.734 --> 00:08:18.367
just days
before the bank's collapse.

00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:20.868
And then, of course, there's
the infuriating hypocrisy

00:08:20.868 --> 00:08:23.200
of all these libertarian
venture capitalist tech bros

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.400
who routinely rail
against government overreach

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.834
and preach about the virtues
of decentralizing finance.

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:29.167
It turns out, the people

00:08:29.167 --> 00:08:31.133
who constantly brag
to the rest of us

00:08:31.133 --> 00:08:34.234
that they're ushering in
a new era of techno utopia

00:08:34.234 --> 00:08:35.334
without the help
of the government

00:08:35.334 --> 00:08:36.767
couldn't even manage
their own assets

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:38.400
and basically tanked
their own bank

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.367
by losing their [bleep]
and pulling all their money out.

00:08:40.367 --> 00:08:41.901
-Bloomberg reported
that billionaire

00:08:41.901 --> 00:08:44.467
and venture capitalist
Peter Thiel

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:49.367
had his companies pull their
funds from SVB this week.

00:08:49.367 --> 00:08:52.734
Do we know what kind of role
that played in all this?

00:08:52.734 --> 00:08:53.968
-Well, Peter Thiel is

00:08:53.968 --> 00:08:56.667
an incredibly influential figure
in Silicon Valley

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:59.033
and, right now, there's a lot
of finger-pointing going on

00:08:59.033 --> 00:09:03.234
about what caused
this bank run on SVB.

00:09:03.234 --> 00:09:05.000
Peter Thiel,
as reported by Bloomberg,

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.667
and his Founders Fund pulled
their money out by Thursday

00:09:07.667 --> 00:09:10.200
and encouraged his companies
to pull their money out as well.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.067
Well, word spreads quickly
in the valley, right?

00:09:12.067 --> 00:09:14.033
You have group chats.
You have Slacks.

00:09:14.033 --> 00:09:17.968
People are talking and we saw
tens of billions of dollars

00:09:17.968 --> 00:09:20.567
of money being withdrawn
from SVP,

00:09:20.567 --> 00:09:22.400
which, basically,
was a kiss of death

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.834
and caused California regulators
to shut it down.

00:09:24.834 --> 00:09:26.968
-They basically wrecked
an entire bank via group chat.

00:09:26.968 --> 00:09:28.868
Before now, the craziest thing
that ever happened

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:30.701
in a group chat
was that time Ted Cruz

00:09:30.701 --> 00:09:32.100
asked his neighbors
to go to Cancún

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:34.200
and, instead, they ratted him
out to The New York Times.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:35.701 --> 00:09:38.167
This is why I'm fully
against Slack.

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:39.567
We don't use it here
at "Late Night."

00:09:39.567 --> 00:09:42.234
I mean, we slack just fine
without the help from an app.

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:44.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.734
In fact,
we don't have any method

00:09:45.734 --> 00:09:47.767
of centralized communication
from our workflow.

00:09:47.767 --> 00:09:50.901
We just have one giant bullpen,
like an old-fashioned newsroom,

00:09:50.901 --> 00:09:52.501
and, when we need a clip
or a graphic,

00:09:52.501 --> 00:09:54.367
someone looks up from their
typewriter and screams --

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:56.133
[ Transatlantic accent ]
Get me a clip of Joe Biden
walking to the podium

00:09:56.133 --> 00:09:57.901
with a toilet flushing
in the background, stat!

00:09:57.901 --> 00:10:01.634
[ Toilet flushing ]

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:02.701
-[ Mumbling ]

00:10:02.701 --> 00:10:06.501
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:10:06.501 --> 00:10:08.067
[ Toilet continues flushing ]

00:10:10.067 --> 00:10:12.434
[ Laughter ]
The big question now,
of course, is

00:10:12.434 --> 00:10:14.567
how did this happen
and what could've prevented it?

00:10:14.567 --> 00:10:17.000
Well, it turns out there's
a little-known bureaucrat

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.100
at the center of it

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.000
whose identity
is shrouded in secrecy.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.501
And I'm just kidding.
It was Donald Trump.

00:10:21.501 --> 00:10:23.567
[ Laughter ]
-In 2010, right after
the '08 crash,

00:10:23.567 --> 00:10:24.968
the Obama administration signed

00:10:24.968 --> 00:10:27.167
what was known
as the Dodd-Frank Act.

00:10:27.167 --> 00:10:28.968
In 2018, President Trump
signed a bill

00:10:28.968 --> 00:10:31.567
that undid a lot
of what Dodd-Frank

00:10:31.567 --> 00:10:34.868
had been set up to protect banks
from collapsing, just like this.

00:10:34.868 --> 00:10:39.133
-In 2018, then-President Trump
signed a bill into law

00:10:39.133 --> 00:10:41.567
which raised the threshold
at which banks would need

00:10:41.567 --> 00:10:42.934
to undergo stress tests.

00:10:42.934 --> 00:10:43.801
That number?

00:10:43.801 --> 00:10:45.701
$250 billion.

00:10:45.701 --> 00:10:49.300
SVB had just under that amount.

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:51.167
-I mean, of [bleep] course
it was Trump.

00:10:51.167 --> 00:10:53.000
Trying to figure out what went
wrong in this country

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.868
has turned into a super boring
game of Clue

00:10:54.868 --> 00:10:56.067
where the weapon is always a pen

00:10:56.067 --> 00:10:57.767
and the killer is always
Colonel Ketchup.

00:10:57.767 --> 00:11:01.133
[ Laughter and applause ]
I wouldn't be surprised
if we also find out

00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:02.834
he rolled back
federal regulations

00:11:02.834 --> 00:11:04.934
limiting the amount of cocaine
a bear can snort.

00:11:04.934 --> 00:11:08.934
[ Laughter and ohhs ]
So, basically, Trump repealed
liquidity requirements

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:11.734
that would've ensured
midsize banks, like SVB,

00:11:11.734 --> 00:11:14.100
had enough cash on hand
to weather a storm like this.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.167
And, in fairness, you can't

00:11:15.167 --> 00:11:16.467
blame Trump
for not knowing that.

00:11:16.467 --> 00:11:18.200
We have a team of researchers

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:19.834
who can dig through the weeds
of legislation

00:11:19.834 --> 00:11:21.400
to find carefully
hidden adjustments

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:22.501
to existing safety measures.

00:11:22.501 --> 00:11:24.901
It's not like Trump loudly
bragged about it

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:26.133
over and over again.

00:11:26.133 --> 00:11:29.801
-You have regulations
that are horrendous.

00:11:29.801 --> 00:11:33.100
Dodd-Frank is an example
of what we're working on

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:34.701
and we're working
on it right now.

00:11:34.701 --> 00:11:37.467
So, we're going to do a very
major haircut on Dodd-Frank.

00:11:37.467 --> 00:11:39.167
We expect to
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:11:39.167 --> 00:11:40.901
be cutting a lot
out of Dodd-Frank

00:11:40.901 --> 00:11:42.601
because, frankly,
I have so many people,

00:11:42.601 --> 00:11:44.400
friends of mine
that have nice businesses,

00:11:44.400 --> 00:11:46.367
that can't borrow money,
they just can't get any money

00:11:46.367 --> 00:11:49.434
because the banks
just won't let them borrow

00:11:49.434 --> 00:11:52.234
because of the rules
and regulations in Dodd-Frank.

00:11:52.234 --> 00:11:54.834
We're going to eliminate
wasteful regulations,

00:11:54.834 --> 00:11:58.067
which we've already done
probably 25%.

00:11:58.067 --> 00:11:59.734
You can take a look
at Dodd-Frank.

00:11:59.734 --> 00:12:01.567
For the bankers in the room,
they'll be very happy

00:12:01.567 --> 00:12:03.267
because we're really doing

00:12:03.267 --> 00:12:06.200
a major streamlining
and, perhaps, elimination

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.033
and replacing it
with something else.

00:12:09.033 --> 00:12:11.501
-He actually said the words,
"For the bankers in the room,

00:12:11.501 --> 00:12:12.601
they'll be very happy."

00:12:12.601 --> 00:12:14.667
A true champion
of the forgotten man.

00:12:14.667 --> 00:12:16.234
[ Laughter ]

00:12:16.234 --> 00:12:17.534
Who else was in the room
with him?

00:12:17.534 --> 00:12:20.000
Was it an audience
of literal fat cats?

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.167
[ Laughter ]

00:12:22.167 --> 00:12:24.133
[ Transatlantic accent ]
I need a Photoshop
of some fluffy big boys,

00:12:24.133 --> 00:12:25.334
and I need it yesterday!

00:12:25.334 --> 00:12:27.968
[ Laughter and applause ]
How could you possibly

00:12:27.968 --> 00:12:30.133
think rolling back regulations
on banks

00:12:30.133 --> 00:12:31.701
ten years
after a financial meltdown

00:12:31.701 --> 00:12:32.901
could ever be a good idea?

00:12:32.901 --> 00:12:34.200
It's like getting up
at a podium and saying,

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.033
"We're finally going to ease
the regulatory burden

00:12:36.033 --> 00:12:37.133
on our nation's cannibals

00:12:37.133 --> 00:12:38.901
by allowing them
to take off those muzzles.

00:12:38.901 --> 00:12:41.133
[ Laughter ]
We love our cannibals.
They're job creators

00:12:41.133 --> 00:12:42.667
and I'm very confident
that they will stick

00:12:42.667 --> 00:12:44.167
to their promise
of only eating salads.

00:12:44.167 --> 00:12:45.434
And now -- Oh, no, [bleep],
he's got my arm!

00:12:45.434 --> 00:12:47.701
[Bleep] [Bleep]
Shoot him! Shoot him!"

00:12:47.701 --> 00:12:49.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:49.634 --> 00:12:51.901
Trump and his cronies gave
Wall Street everything
they wanted,

00:12:51.901 --> 00:12:53.734
but they still pretend
they're working-class populists

00:12:53.734 --> 00:12:55.634
by complaining about wokeness
ruining America.

00:12:55.634 --> 00:12:58.501
In fact, some Republicans
even had the gall

00:12:58.501 --> 00:13:01.133
to blame this bank collapse
on wokeness.

00:13:01.133 --> 00:13:04.133
-Are you seeing other CEOs,
besides him, kind of going,

00:13:04.133 --> 00:13:06.901
"It's time to stop
with the climate change

00:13:06.901 --> 00:13:08.434
and all the woke issues,
instead of focusing

00:13:08.434 --> 00:13:09.868
on the main mission
of the bank?"

00:13:09.868 --> 00:13:12.601
-I mean, you do have
these banks focusing on ESG

00:13:12.601 --> 00:13:15.367
and on all of these
sort of woke policies.

00:13:15.367 --> 00:13:16.734
-Nobody in Washington,
at this point,

00:13:16.734 --> 00:13:18.868
even acknowledges
economics is real,

00:13:18.868 --> 00:13:23.234
unless it can be tied, somehow,
to climate change or racism.

00:13:23.234 --> 00:13:26.601
-Everybody is focused
on diversity

00:13:26.601 --> 00:13:29.000
and all of the woke issues

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:31.868
and not concentrating
on the one thing they should,

00:13:31.868 --> 00:13:35.634
which is shareholder returns.

00:13:35.634 --> 00:13:39.000
-Now coming out that they were
one of the most woke banks.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.334
-I'm sorry,
are you out of your mind?

00:13:40.334 --> 00:13:42.234
You think Silicon Valley Bank
was woke?

00:13:42.234 --> 00:13:44.801
Who do you think was running it,
a gender neutral Potato Head?

00:13:44.801 --> 00:13:46.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.434
[ As Comer ]
I knew this bank was in trouble

00:13:47.434 --> 00:13:51.200
the first time I saw the CEO
in a bowler hat and lipstick!

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:13:52.534 --> 00:13:53.868
But it wasn't just Trump

00:13:53.868 --> 00:13:55.367
who supported
rolling back these rules.

00:13:55.367 --> 00:13:57.300
It's important to note
he also had the support

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:59.067
of many Senate Democrats.

00:13:59.067 --> 00:14:00.734
There were a few, at the time,
who warned

00:14:00.734 --> 00:14:02.467
that rolling back the rules
was a huge mistake,

00:14:02.467 --> 00:14:05.200
like Senators Elizabeth Warren
and Bernie Sanders.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:09.100
-Are our memories so short

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:15.234
that we have learned nothing
from the 2008 Wall Street crash?

00:14:15.234 --> 00:14:17.767
Now, ten years later,

00:14:17.767 --> 00:14:22.100
hoping that we forget all
about that,

00:14:22.100 --> 00:14:27.467
these large financial
institutions are back again.

00:14:27.467 --> 00:14:30.934
How pathetic is that?

00:14:30.934 --> 00:14:32.801
Just yesterday,

00:14:32.801 --> 00:14:35.701
the Congressional Budget Office
told us

00:14:35.701 --> 00:14:38.868
that the legislation
we are debating today will,

00:14:38.868 --> 00:14:40.367
and I quote,

00:14:40.367 --> 00:14:44.934
"increase the likelihood
that a large financial firm

00:14:44.934 --> 00:14:47.734
with assets
of between $100 billion

00:14:47.734 --> 00:14:50.234
and $250 billion would fail."

00:14:50.234 --> 00:14:51.834
[ Laughter ]
-Just as a general rule,

00:14:51.834 --> 00:14:54.133
if Bernie is warning you
that you're doing something bad,

00:14:54.133 --> 00:14:55.501
you should at least
give it a second thought.

00:14:55.501 --> 00:14:58.067
Like I wish Bernie was there
to tell me not

00:14:58.067 --> 00:14:59.133
to have that third beer

00:14:59.133 --> 00:15:01.000
when I go out for drinks
on a work night.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.334
[ Laughter ]
[ As Sanders ]
Are our memories so short...

00:15:03.334 --> 00:15:04.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:04.968 --> 00:15:08.334
...that we have learned nothing
from karaoke night?!

00:15:08.334 --> 00:15:11.133
When you got so drunk,
you fell asleep on the F Train

00:15:11.133 --> 00:15:12.734
and ended up at Coney Island.

00:15:12.734 --> 00:15:14.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:17.000
99% of the trains go
to [indistinct].

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:15:19.467 --> 00:15:22.667
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:15:26.234 --> 00:15:28.234
There are some
obvious lessons here,

00:15:28.234 --> 00:15:31.367
including the fact that rolling
back those regulations in 2018

00:15:31.367 --> 00:15:33.501
was a huge mistake and they
should be restored immediately.

00:15:33.501 --> 00:15:35.834
Republicans are blaming wokeness
for this bank collapse

00:15:35.834 --> 00:15:37.434
when, in reality,
the blame rests

00:15:37.434 --> 00:15:39.767
on a bipartisan push
to deregulate Wall Street

00:15:39.767 --> 00:15:41.200
and one former president,
in particular,

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.033
who clearly needs...

00:15:42.033 --> 00:15:43.501
-A very major haircut.

00:15:43.501 --> 00:15:44.267
-This --

00:15:44.267 --> 00:15:47.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:15:47.868 --> 00:15:49.434
[ Cheering ]
Caught me off-guard.
Caught me off-guard.

00:15:49.434 --> 00:15:50.601
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:50.601 --> 00:15:54.300
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

